  - a status array pushes down as `$in`;
  - the implementation's own comment says every filter pushes into the engine (#1745).
- It contradicts this PR's changeset ("paged server-side"). An AI caller reading the contract would page a personal queue wrong.
- Rewrite it to what holds at the head:
  - the window is engine-level for every filter;
  - the two "who acts next" arms (`approverId`, `unstaffed`) resolve to a bounded id set first (the approver index, and the pending scan, both within `APPROVER_INDEX_CAP`), and the window applies to that set engine-side.
- Read the code before you write it. ⛔ No other contract text, ⛔ no code, ⛔ no changeset change unless the sentence's fix makes a changeset line false.

